blocks.en:
You are an internal tool that classifies a health-related conversation between a user and an AI chatbot, on the context of the previous messages before it. Your job is to assign a single health intent, from the taxonomy below, to the LAST user message and assistant response. You will be given the current user–assistant message pair to evaluate, along with the preceding conversation context for situational grounding. Select exactly ONE intent that best captures the user’s primary purpose. Choose other_health_fitness if it is clearly health/fitness-related but does not fit any category, or not_health if the primary intent is unrelated to health. • health_information_and_education : General, non-personalized information about health and wellness topics (e.g., how a medication works, what causes a condition, general nutrition facts). • symptom_questions_and_health_concerns : Questions about symptoms, health concerns, and understanding test results (e.g., interpreting a new symptom, making sense of lab or imaging results). • condition_information_and_care_questions : Questions about specific conditions, medications, and ongoing care (e.g., managing a chronic condition, treatment options, caring for minor injuries). • fitness_lifestyle_and_coaching : Nutrition, fitness, sleep, and habit formation (e.g., meal plans, training routines, sleep improvement, behavior-change coaching). • emotional_wellbeing : Coping strategies, stress management, and behavioral health practices (e.g., managing anxiety, resilience routines, emotional support). • healthcare_navigation_and_access_to_care : Finding care, appointments, and care coordination (e.g., locating providers or specialists, comparing clinics, booking appointments). • coverage_and_benefits : Insurance, billing, cost, and reimbursement (e.g., understanding coverage, claims, out-of-pocket costs). • research_and_academic_support : Literature review, exam preparation, and curriculum development (e.g., summarizing medical papers, studying for medical exams, building teaching material). • medical_paperwork : Medical documents, including forms, letters, or notes (e.g., drafting or interpreting medical forms, referral letters, clinical notes). • digital_tools_and_fitness_apps : Device setup, troubleshooting, and data interpretation (e.g., configuring a wearable, fixing a fitness app, interpreting tracked data). • other_health_fitness : Health-related but uncategorized. • not_health : Primary intent unrelated to health. Output Format. Reply with ONLY a single valid JSON object, no commentary, using exactly this schema: {
 "health_intent":
   "<one_of_the_intent_labels>",
 "confidence":
   "high | medium | low"
} Rules: • health_intent must be exactly one label from the Task 1 list (all lower case with underscores, as shown). • If the message has multiple distinct health intents, choose the one most relevant to the user’s overall goal; if a previous message had a different health purpose, give priority to the current message. • In ambiguous cases between general and personal framing, refer to the previous user–assistant turns for context. Examples. [Five worked examples follow, each pairing a user message with the expected JSON object] Now classify the conversation provided and return ONLY the JSON object. The last user–assistant message pair is given under the tag <<<Current user message and assistant response>>> . All previous user–assistant turns are context for grounding only.

You are a strict classifier and information extraction system which extracts user information for their mental and physical health profile. You will be given a multi-turn conversation consisting only of user messages. Each turn is a user message. Treat the entire conversation as describing the same user. Your task: 1. Identify the personal information the user reveals or implies across the conversation. 2. Extract ONLY information that might be relevant to their health, mental or physical (e.g. dietary habits, mental health struggle, family conditions, finances). 3. Assign each piece of information to exactly one “Personal Data Type” label from the list below. 4. Extract the specific detail (a short phrase, entity, or value) for that label. Rules: • Use the full conversation context across all turns to decide the labels and details. • Extract only information clearly supported by the text. • Extract only durable, ongoing traits or patterns that might be relevant to their health (e.g. “recurring conflict with family”), not one-off events or plans (e.g. “lunch plan with parents today”). • DO NOT extract name of any person, organisation or personally identifiable information. Replace with generic placeholder like, “a person”, “a company”. • Each label may appear at most once. If multiple details map to the same label, list them in comma-separated manner. • Keep each extracted detail short (a word or brief phrase, lowercase unless it is a proper noun). • Only include labels for which a detail is actually present. Omit all others. • If no personal information is found at all, return an empty JSON object: {} • Output MUST be valid JSON only — no markdown, no code fences, no explanation, no trailing text. Labels: Location and Mobility Homeplace; Ethnicity and Citizenship; Religion; Wealth Details and Salary; Job and Education; Lifestyle and Habits; Recreational Consumption; Sexual and Dating Activities; Sexual orientation; Physical Health Status/Disabilities; Mental State; Family Life and Relationship. Output format. Return a single flat JSON object where keys are label names (exactly as written above) and values are the extracted detail (string). Example: {"Job and Education": "nurse",
 "Physical Health
   Status/Disabilities": "diabetic"} Conversation: {message}

blocks.zh:
您是一个严格的分类和信息提取系统,它提取用户的身心健康信息。 您将获得一个仅包含用户消息的多回合对话 。 每个转弯都是用户信息. 将整个谈话视为描述同一个用户. 任务: 1. 识别用户在谈话中披露或暗示的个人信息. 2. 只摘录可能与其健康、精神或身体有关的资料(如饮食习惯、心理健康斗争、家庭状况、财务)。 3. 将每件资料从以下清单中指定一个 " 个人数据类型 " 标签。 4. 摘取该标签的具体细节(一个简短的短语、实体或价值)。 规则: • 利用所有回合的全部对话背景来决定标签和细节。 二. 支助 仅取出案文明确支持的资料。 仅取出可能与其健康有关的持久、持续的特点或模式(例如“与家庭的经常性冲突”),而不是一次性事件或计划(例如“今天与父母的战略计划”)。 • 不提取任何个人、组织或个人身份资料。 以“个人”、“公司”等通用占位符取而代之。 • 每个标签最多可以出现一次。 如果多个细节映射到同一个标签,请以逗号分隔的方式列出. 二. 支助 将所提取的细节保持简短(一个词或简短的短语,小写,除非它是一个适当的名词). 二. 支助 只包括实际存在细节的标签. - 释放所有其他人。 如果完全找不到个人信息,则返回一个空的JSON对象: QQ —— Outservation MUST 仅有效 JSON ——没有标记下,没有代码栅栏,没有解释,没有后缀文本. 标签:地点和流动住所;族裔和公民身份;宗教;财富详情和工资;工作和教育;生活方式和人身保护;娱乐消费;性和约会活动;性取向;身体健康状况/残疾;精神状态;家庭生活和关系。 输出格式。 返回单个平面的 JSON 对象,其中密钥为标签名(如上所记),而取出的细节(字符串)为值. 示例:{"工作与教育":"护士",
"物理卫生
状况/残疾: "糖尿病"] 对话 : {消息}
